      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary vasospasm is one cause of chest pain in patients with acute myocarditis. This is a rare association, with few cases reported in the literature. The authors describe a case of acute myocarditis in which presentation mimicked acute myocardial infarction. During hospitalization severe angina recurred twice, accompanied by transient ST-segment elevation in different locations. The hypothesis of coronary vasospasm is discussed. The role of cardiac magnetic resonance imaging in this context is highlighted."},
